p.src:
The advantage is visible in the number-operator matrix element $\langle n\rvert a^\dagger a\lvert n\rangle.$ Acting to the right, $\begin{aligned}
a\lvert n\rangle&=\sqrt n\,\lvert n-1\rangle,\\
a^\dagger\lvert n-1\rangle&=\sqrt n\,\lvert n\rangle,\end{aligned}$ so $\langle n\rvert a^\dagger a\lvert n\rangle
=n\langle n\vert n\rangle=n.$ Acting instead to the left, $\begin{aligned}
\langle n\rvert a^\dagger&=\sqrt n\,\langle n-1\rvert,\\
\langle n-1\rvert a&=\sqrt n\,\langle n\rvert,\end{aligned}$ and the same answer follows. One need not decide which direction is more fundamental; the calculus is arranged so that either direction gives the same number.

