p.src:
Adopt the convention that $\psi$ annihilates and $\psi^\dagger$ creates: $\begin{aligned}
\psi(x)&=\sum_k a(k)e^{ikx},\\
\psi^\dagger(x)&=\sum_k a^\dagger(k)e^{-ikx}.\end{aligned}$ The sum is over $k=2\pi n/L$ in periodic space and becomes continuous in infinite space. The second equation is the Hermitian conjugate of the first. It may also be thought of as the operator analogue of a complex conjugate.

