p.src:
So far the fields depend on position but not time. Fields oscillate, and each wave number $k$ has an associated frequency $\omega(k)$. An object of definite frequency $\omega$ has time dependence $e^{i\omega t}=\cos(\omega t)+i\sin(\omega t).$ Attach the conjugate phases to the two field expansions: $\begin{aligned}
\psi(x,t)&=\sum_k a(k)e^{ikx}e^{-i\omega(k)t},\\
\psi^\dagger(x,t)&=\sum_k a^\dagger(k)e^{-ikx}e^{i\omega(k)t}.\end{aligned}$ Now each spatial mode oscillates at the frequency appropriate to its wave number, and the field depends on both space and time.

