p.src:
Multiplying the time derivative by $i$ gives the same mode coefficient as dividing the second spatial derivative by $2m$: $\begin{aligned}
i\dot\psi^\dagger
&=-\sum_k\omega(k)a^\dagger(k)e^{-ikx}e^{i\omega(k)t},\\
\frac{1}{2m}\frac{\partial^2\psi^\dagger}{\partial x^2}
&=-\sum_k\omega(k)a^\dagger(k)e^{-ikx}e^{i\omega(k)t}.\end{aligned}$ Hence $i\frac{\partial\psi^\dagger}{\partial t}
=\frac{1}{2m}\frac{\partial^2\psi^\dagger}{\partial x^2},$ or, equivalently, $-i\frac{\partial\psi^\dagger}{\partial t}
=-\frac{1}{2m}\frac{\partial^2\psi^\dagger}{\partial x^2}.$

