The origin $x=0$ was chosen only for convenience. Put the target at $x=x_{\mathrm T}$. The spatial factors in $\psi^\dagger(x_{\mathrm T},t)\psi(x_{\mathrm T},t)$ give $e^{-ik_f x_{\mathrm T}}e^{ik_i x_{\mathrm T}}
=e^{i(k_i-k_f)x_{\mathrm T}}.$ Thus the amplitude becomes $\mathcal A_{i\to f}(x_{\mathrm T})
=e^{i(k_i-k_f)x_{\mathrm T}}
\mathcal A_{i\to f}(0).$

