Now reverse the asymmetry. Suppose an interaction could occur at any position but only at one distinguished time. An integral over position would give $\int_{-\infty}^{\infty}dx\,
e^{i(k_i-k_f)x}
=2\pi\delta(k_i-k_f),$ while fixing the time would remove the energy delta function.

